## Proposed Architecture & Phases

Since this is a massive platform expansion, we will break the execution down into logical phases.

### Phase 1: Enhanced Database Models (MongoDB)
We will expand the Node.js/MongoDB backend to track all the data the AI needs.

#### [MODIFY] `server/models/User.js`
- Add fields for `streak`, `last_active`, `weak_topics`, `mentor_notes`, and a `progress` sub-document.

#### [NEW] `server/models/Roadmap.js`
- A new model to store AI-generated daily tasks and weekly milestones for each user.

### Phase 2: Main Agent & Intent Detection (Workflow 1 & 6)
We will rebuild the primary `n8n-ai-mentor-workflow.json`.

#### [MODIFY] `n8n-ai-mentor-workflow.json`
- We will add an **Intent Classifier** node right after the Webhook.
- Based on intent, it will route to: Doubt Clarification, Roadmap Generator, or Code Help.
- Add an HTTP Request node to fetch the user's `User.js` profile and learning history from the Node.js backend *before* answering.

### Phase 3: The Code Mentor Flow (Workflow 3)
We already have an AI Code IDE page in the platform.

#### [MODIFY] `src/pages/AICodeIDE.tsx` (or similar)
- Re-route the code submission logic to hit a specific n8n webhook (`/webhook/code-mentor`).

#### [NEW] `n8n-code-mentor-workflow.json`
- Build the n8n blueprint that analyzes code syntax and ONLY returns hints (max 10-15 lines of code examples).

### Phase 4: Roadmap & Progress Workflows (Workflows 2 & 4)

#### [NEW] `n8n-roadmap-workflow.json`
- Input: Goal, Level, Time. Output: Structured JSON roadmap.

#### [NEW] `n8n-progress-workflow.json`
- An n8n webhook triggered by the Node backend every time a user finishes a quiz/lesson.
- Updates the `progress` field and returns an AI insight for the user's dashboard.

### Phase 5: Reminder System (Workflow 5)

#### [NEW] `n8n-cron-reminder-workflow.json`
- A schedule trigger node set to run daily at 8 PM.
- Pulls inactive users from MongoDB, generates an encouraging message, and pushes it out.

